<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Vescera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">682</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Tahuda · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-the-maghreb">Muslim conquest of the Maghreb</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Vescera was fought near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biskra">Biskra</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> in 682 or 683, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kusaila">Kusaila</a>, with Byzantine support, ambushed the Arab commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uqba-ibn-nafi">Uqba ibn Nafi</a> as he returned from a campaign that had reached the Atlantic. Uqba and most of his escort were killed at Tahuda. The defeat let Kusaila take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> and delayed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-the-maghreb">Muslim conquest of the Maghreb</a> for several years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vescera.jpg" alt="Battle of Vescera" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hydrosami · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_ruins_of_THOUDA_Biskra_Algeria_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
